---
const defaultL = 2;
const defaultXi = 0.2;
const lsPlus = defaultL / 2;
const lsMinus = -(defaultL + 1) / 2;
---

<figure
  class="chapter-visual spin-orbit-explorer"
  data-spin-orbit
  data-normalized-operator="LdotS-over-hbar2"
  data-xi-unit="energy"
>
  <figcaption>
    <strong>原创教学模型：$\mathbf L\cdot\mathbf S$ 分裂 | Original teaching model: $\mathbf L\cdot\mathbf S$ splitting</strong>
    <span>模型 Hamiltonian 为 $H_{\mathrm{SO}}^{\mathrm{model}}=\xi(\mathbf L\cdot\mathbf S/\hbar^2)$，采用单电子 $s=1/2$，其中 $\xi$ 以能量为单位。</span>
    <span lang="en">The model Hamiltonian is $H_{\mathrm{SO}}^{\mathrm{model}}=\xi(\mathbf L\cdot\mathbf S/\hbar^2)$ for one electron with $s=1/2$, with $\xi$ in energy units.</span>
  </figcaption>

  <div class="chapter-visual__controls">
    <label>
      <span>轨道角动量 $l$: <output data-l-output>{defaultL}</output></span>
      <input data-l type="range" min="0" max="5" step="1" value={defaultL} aria-label="Orbital angular momentum l" />
    </label>
    <label>
      <span>耦合能量 $\xi$: <output data-xi-output>{defaultXi.toFixed(2)}</output> eV</span>
      <input data-xi type="range" min="-1" max="1" step="0.05" value={defaultXi} aria-label="Spin orbit coupling energy xi in electron volts" />
    </label>
  </div>

  <svg viewBox="0 0 760 300" role="img" aria-labelledby="soc-title soc-desc">
    <title id="soc-title">Spin orbit splitting into j equals l plus or minus one half</title>
    <desc id="soc-desc">Energy levels from the dimensionless L dot S over hbar squared eigenvalues, with degeneracies two j plus one.</desc>
    <line class="soc-centre" x1="90" y1="150" x2="670" y2="150" />
    <line data-plus-line class="soc-level soc-plus" x1="390" y1="120" x2="650" y2="120" />
    <line data-minus-line class="soc-level soc-minus" x1="110" y1="195" x2="370" y2="195" />
    <text x="100" y="143">unsplit centre</text>
    <text data-plus-label x="520" y="105" text-anchor="middle">j=5/2, g=6, ΔE=+0.200 eV</text>
    <text data-minus-label x="240" y="220" text-anchor="middle">j=3/2, g=4, ΔE=−0.300 eV</text>
  </svg>

  <p class="chapter-visual__readout" aria-live="polite">
    <span>〈L·S/ℏ²〉 for j = l + 1/2 = <strong data-ls-plus>{lsPlus.toFixed(2)}</strong></span>
    <span>〈L·S/ℏ²〉 for j = l − 1/2 = <strong data-ls-minus>{lsMinus.toFixed(2)}</strong></span>
    <span>简并度加权迹：<strong data-trace>0.000000</strong> eV</span>
  </p>

  <div class="chapter-visual__contract">
    <p><strong>验收：</strong>对 $l>0$，无量纲算符 $\mathbf L\cdot\mathbf S/\hbar^2$ 的两支本征值分别为 $l/2$ 和 $-(l+1)/2$；用简并度 $2j+1$ 加权后，完整 $l\otimes s$ 空间中的能量迹为零。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Acceptance:</strong> for $l>0$, the two eigenvalues of the dimensionless operator $\mathbf L\cdot\mathbf S/\hbar^2$ are $l/2$ and $-(l+1)/2$; weighting by degeneracy $2j+1$ gives zero energy trace over the complete $l\otimes s$ space.</p>
    <p><strong>边界：</strong>$\xi$ 在此模型中是能量；若直接把 Hamiltonian 写成 $\tilde\xi\,\mathbf L\cdot\mathbf S$，则 $\tilde\xi$ 必须具有 eV/$\hbar^2$ 的量纲。真实原子的耦合还取决于径向势梯度、径向波函数、壳层和化学环境；此图不包含晶场或多电子多重态。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Boundary:</strong> $\xi$ is an energy in this model. A Hamiltonian written directly as $\tilde\xi\,\mathbf L\cdot\mathbf S$ requires $\tilde\xi$ to have units of eV/$\hbar^2$. The physical atomic coupling also depends on the radial potential gradient, radial wavefunction, shell, and environment; the figure omits crystal fields and many-electron multiplets.</p>
  </div>

  <noscript><p>无 JavaScript 时显示默认 $l=2$、$\xi=0.20$ eV 的解析分裂，并采用 $\mathbf L\cdot\mathbf S/\hbar^2$ 无量纲算符。</p></noscript>
</figure>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-spin-orbit]').forEach((root) => {
    const lInput = root.querySelector('[data-l]');
    const xiInput = root.querySelector('[data-xi]');
    const update = () => {
      const l = Number(lInput.value);
      const xi = Number(xiInput.value);
      const plusExists = l >= 0;
      const minusExists = l > 0;
      const lsPlus = l / 2;
      const lsMinus = -(l + 1) / 2;
      const ePlus = xi * lsPlus;
      const eMinus = xi * lsMinus;
      const scale = 85;
      const yPlus = 150 - Math.max(-1.2, Math.min(1.2, ePlus)) * scale;
      const yMinus = 150 - Math.max(-1.2, Math.min(1.2, eMinus)) * scale;
      root.querySelector('[data-plus-line]').setAttribute('y1', String(yPlus));
      root.querySelector('[data-plus-line]').setAttribute('y2', String(yPlus));
      root.querySelector('[data-minus-line]').setAttribute('y1', String(yMinus));
      root.querySelector('[data-minus-line]').setAttribute('y2', String(yMinus));
      root.querySelector('[data-minus-line]').style.display = minusExists ? '' : 'none';
      root.querySelector('[data-minus-label]').style.display = minusExists ? '' : 'none';
      const jPlus = l + 0.5;
      const jMinus = l - 0.5;
      const gPlus = 2 * l + 2;
      const gMinus = 2 * l;
      root.querySelector('[data-plus-label]').textContent = `j=${jPlus}, g=${gPlus}, ΔE=${ePlus >= 0 ? '+' : ''}${ePlus.toFixed(3)} eV`;
      root.querySelector('[data-minus-label]').textContent = `j=${jMinus}, g=${gMinus}, ΔE=${eMinus >= 0 ? '+' : ''}${eMinus.toFixed(3)} eV`;
      root.querySelector('[data-l-output]').textContent = String(l);
      root.querySelector('[data-xi-output]').textContent = xi.toFixed(2);
      root.querySelector('[data-ls-plus]').textContent = lsPlus.toFixed(2);
      root.querySelector('[data-ls-minus]').textContent = minusExists ? lsMinus.toFixed(2) : 'not present';
      const trace = plusExists ? gPlus * ePlus + (minusExists ? gMinus * eMinus : 0) : 0;
      const normalizedTrace = Math.abs(trace) < 1e-12 ? 0 : trace;
      root.querySelector('[data-trace]').textContent = normalizedTrace.toFixed(6);
    };
    lInput.addEventListener('input', update);
    xiInput.addEventListener('input', update);
    update();
  });
</script>

<style>
  .spin-orbit-explorer svg {
    width: 100%;
    min-height: 15rem;
  }

  .spin-orbit-explorer svg text {
    fill: currentColor;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .soc-centre {
    stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-4);
    stroke-dasharray: 6 5;
  }

  .soc-level {
    stroke-width: 5;
  }

  .soc-plus { stroke: #3273dc; }
  .soc-minus { stroke: #d97706; }
</style>
